---
import LetsTalk from '@components/home/LetsTalk.astro'
import Insight from '@components/insights/Insight.astro'
import InsightSignoff from '@components/insights/InsightSignoff.astro'
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
import { getInsightNav } from '@data/insights'
import InsightNav from '@components/insights/InsightNav.astro'

const { previous, current, next } = getInsightNav('what-is-aeo-and-is-it-replacing-seo')
---

<Layout title={current?.title} description={current?.summary}>
  <Insight tags={current?.tags}>
    <span slot="insight-title">{current?.title}</span>
    <span slot="insight-subtitle">{current?.dateLabel}</span>
    <span slot="insight-text">
      <p>
        We are not an SEO company, but we find that our clients are increasingly asking us about this: AEO is not
        replacing SEO, it is building on top of it. If you are optimising for one and ignoring the other, you are being
        overtaken.
      </p><br />
      <p>
        Answer Engine Optimization is the practice of structuring content so that AI answer engines, Google's AI
        Overviews, ChatGPT Search, etc., can pull it directly into a synthesised answer rather than just linking to it
        [1]. Traditional SEO still works at the page level: titles, keywords, backlinks, getting a page to rank. AEO
        works closer to the fact level: clear definitions, citable statistics, and sections structured so an AI system
        can lift them out cleanly and attribute them back to you [2]. This matters because a large and growing share of
        searches now end without a single click, with AI-generated answers satisfying the query directly on the results
        page [3].
      </p><br />
      <p>
        The practical takeaway is not to abandon your existing SEO work and chase AEO instead. It is to make sure your
        content is written in a way that both a search engine and an AI system can use: clear structure, direct answers
        near the top, facts stated plainly enough to be quoted. If your website content still reads like it was written
        purely to rank rather than to actually answer a question, that is the gap worth closing first.
      </p><br />
      <p><strong>Citations:</strong></p><br />
      <ul class="lg:mt-4 flex flex-col gap-4">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            [1] <a
              href="https://cxl.com/blog/answer-engine-optimization-aeo-the-comprehensive-guide/"
              class="underline underline-offset-2"
              target="_blank">Answer Engine Optimization (AEO): The Comprehensive Guide</a
            >
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            [2] <a
              href="https://www.frase.io/blog/what-is-answer-engine-optimization-the-complete-guide-to-getting-cited-by-ai"
              class="underline underline-offset-2"
              target="_blank">What Is Answer Engine Optimization</a
            >
          </span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
          <span class="shrink-0 w-3 h-3 mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-1.25" style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
          <span>
            [3] <a
              href="https://writer.com/blog/geo-aeo-optimization/"
              class="underline underline-offset-2"
              target="_blank">GEO, AEO, and SEO in 2026: The Enterprise Guide to AI Visibility</a
            >
          </span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <br />
      <InsightSignoff />
    </span>
  </Insight>

  <InsightNav previousInsight={previous} nextInsight={next} />

  <LetsTalk config={{ buttons: 'both', primaryCta: 'message' }} />
</Layout>
